<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Minstrel Boy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">published <a href="/years/1813">1813</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;The Minstrel Boy&quot; is an Irish song by the poet Thomas Moore (1779–1852), published in 1813 in his Irish Melodies, a project that ran from 1808 to 1834. It is set to an air called &quot;The Moreen&quot;, which Moore said was traditional, but his publication of 1813 is the first record of the tune and the only source for that statement; the scholars who have studied his sources have traced no earlier one.</p></div>
